---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Doc from '../components/Doc.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Amplifly terms of service."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of service" lead="The agreement for using Amplifly, in plain language where we can manage it.">
    <p class="small">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    <p class="small">Questions? <a class="link" href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me">hello@amplifly.me</a></p>
  </PageHead>

  <Doc>

      <section id="acceptance">
        <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
        <p>
          By downloading or using Amplifly, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not
          agree, do not use the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-amplifly-is">
        <h2>2. What Amplifly is</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly is a personal productivity and self-understanding tool designed for
          neurodivergent individuals. It is <strong>not a medical device</strong> and is not
          intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any condition. Nothing in Amplifly
          constitutes medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional for
          any health-related questions or decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app is currently listed on the App Store as "Amplifly Lite", the software-only
          release. These terms apply to it under either name. A BioProxal wearable integration is
          in development and is not part of the current release; these terms will be updated
          before a wearable-enabled version is offered.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-account">
        <h2>3. Your account</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly requires an account to use. You are responsible for maintaining the security
          of your credentials and for providing an email address you control. Notify us immediately at{' '}
          <a href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me">hello@amplifly.me</a>{' '}
          if you suspect unauthorized access.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may delete your account at any time by emailing us. We will remove all associated
          data from Supabase within 7 days of your request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="pricing">
        <h2>4. Pricing</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly is a paid application. The current price is $2.99 (USD), as shown on the
          App Store at the point of download, and any purchase is processed by Apple under its
          own terms. All features — brain check-ins, conditions, flow logging, the Focus timer,
          the recommender, and the operating manual — are included, and the account required to
          use the app, along with its cross-device sync, carries no additional charge.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we change pricing or introduce additional paid features in the future, the current
          terms will be reflected on the App Store before you purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="user-responsibilities">
        <h2>5. User responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Use Amplifly only for lawful personal purposes.</li>
          <li>Do not attempt to reverse engineer, decompile, or tamper with the app.</li>
          <li>Do not attempt to gain unauthorized access to any backend infrastructure.</li>
          <li>You are responsible for the content you enter (notes, activity descriptions, etc.).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="intellectual-property">
        <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          All app code, design, copy, and algorithms are owned by Amplifly. Your personal data
          (check-ins, sessions, profile) belongs to you. We claim no ownership over the content
          you create within the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="disclaimer-of-warranties">
        <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
          We do not warrant that the app will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that any
          recommendation will produce a particular outcome.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="limitation-of-liability">
        <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Amplifly and its founders shall not be
          liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use
          of the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes-to-these-terms">
        <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated
          via in-app notice. Continued use of Amplifly after changes constitutes acceptance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms?{' '}
          <a href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me">hello@amplifly.me</a>
        </p>
      </section>

  </Doc>


  <Footer />
</Layout>
